==Trivia==
*Cats of a Common Sea's Japanese name, Warera Umi no Neko (われら海の猫, "We Are Cats of the Sea"), is a pun on the children's song "[[wikipedia:ja:われは海の子|Ware wa Umi no Ko]]" (われは海の子, "I Am a Kid of the Sea").
*All six stages contain aquatic or semiaquatic animals, including hippos, garden eels, squid, ducks, seals, sea otters and [[wikipedia:Sea angel|sea angels]].

